From c12337dfea29b4266e615c917e1cd349fc9be759 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: HuJK <s920361@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 16 Jul 2026 15:38:04 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 5/5] virtio-gpu: don't detach resources from a context the
 host never saw

On devices with VIRTIO_GPU_F_CONTEXT_INIT, virtio_gpu_gem_object_open()
only creates a host context / attaches the resource once userspace has
issued DRM_IOCTL_VIRTGPU_CONTEXT_INIT (vfpriv->context_created).
virtio_gpu_gem_object_close() has no such check, so any DRM fd that
holds GEM handles without ever initializing a 3D context (KMS-only fds
with dumb cursor/scanout BOs: mutter, plymouth, Xwayland teardown, ...)
sends CTX_DETACH_RESOURCE with a ctx_id the host never created.

Hosts that validate the id (crosvm/rutabaga) reply with an error:

  [drm:virtio_gpu_dequeue_ctrl_func [virtio_gpu]] *ERROR* response 0x1200 (command 0x203)

i.e. VIRTIO_GPU_RESP_ERR_UNSPEC for VIRTIO_GPU_CMD_CTX_DETACH_RESOURCE
(crosvm logs CtxDetachResource: ErrRutabaga(InvalidContextId)), once per
GEM handle close on such fds. QEMU+virglrenderer merely ignores the
bogus detach silently. Verified with kprobe tracing on a GNOME guest:
every failing detach came from an fd whose ctx_id had no matching
context create, while interleaved detaches on CONTEXT_INIT'd fds of the
same process succeeded.

Mirror the open() condition in close(): nothing was attached, so there
is nothing to detach.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/virtio/virtgpu_gem.c | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/virtio/virtgpu_gem.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/virtio/virtgpu_gem.c
index f22dc5c..6504edf 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/virtio/virtgpu_gem.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/virtio/virtgpu_gem.c
@@ -139,6 +139,15 @@ void virtio_gpu_gem_object_close(struct drm_gem_object *obj,
 	if (!vgdev->has_virgl_3d)
 		return;
 
+	/* If this file never created a host context (context_init devices only
+	 * get one via DRM_IOCTL_VIRTGPU_CONTEXT_INIT), nothing was ever
+	 * attached: gem_object_open skips the attach for the same reason, and
+	 * a detach would name a ctx_id the host has never seen (crosvm answers
+	 * VIRTIO_GPU_RESP_ERR_UNSPEC, spamming dmesg on every handle close).
+	 */
+	if (!vfpriv->context_created)
+		return;
+
 	objs = virtio_gpu_array_alloc(1);
 	if (!objs)
 		return;
